Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix(sokol):=20draw=5Frectangle=5Frounded=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20no=20degenerate=20triangle=20on=20sharp=20corners?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

emit_corner_arc's radius<=0 (sharp corner) branch emitted a 2-vertex sgl
triangle (center + corner point, no third vertex) — a degenerate primitive that
rendered as a diagonal slice on any MIXED round/sharp corner config (e.g. a
rounded-top tab: top_round()). The four edge triangles + center fan already run
to the exact corner point, so a square corner is fully tiled without the arc —
the sharp branch must emit nothing. Fix: return early.

Proven against hanabi (rounded-top tabs render clean, no notch).
---
 src/backends/sokol/drawing_helpers.h | 15 ++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/sokol/drawing_helpers.h b/src/backends/sokol/drawing_helpers.h
index d08ef1e..2c63083 100644
--- a/src/backends/sokol/drawing_helpers.h
+++ b/src/backends/sokol/drawing_helpers.h
@@ -143,13 +143,14 @@ inline void draw_rectangle_rounded(
   auto emit_corner_arc = [&](float cornerX, float cornerY, float radius,
                              float startAngle) {
     if (radius <= 0.0f) {
-      // Sharp corner: just one triangle from center to corner point
-      sgl_begin_triangles();
-      metal_draw_detail::set_color(color);
-      sgl_v2f(cx, cy);
-      sgl_v2f(cornerX, cornerY);
-      // We'll handle connectivity outside
-      sgl_end();
+      // Sharp corner: emit NOTHING. The four edge triangles below already run
+      // to the exact corner point (e.g. the top + left edges both include
+      // (x,y) when rTL==0), so together with the center fan they fully tile a
+      // square corner. The previous code emitted a 2-vertex sgl triangle here
+      // (cx,cy + cornerX,cornerY and no third vertex) — a DEGENERATE primitive
+      // that rendered as a diagonal "triangle" slice on any MIXED round/sharp
+      // corner config (e.g. rounded-top tabs). Returning is correct + removes
+      // the glitch. (hanabi gap #25)
       return;
     }
     for (int i = 0; i < segs; i++) {
